  "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\n\n### Electron Version\n\n44.2.0\n\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System Version\n\nWindows 10 22H2 and Windows 11 25H2\n\n### What arch are you using?\n\nx64\n\n### Last Known Working Electron version\n\n43.X.X\n\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\n\nNo\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\n`app.commandLine.appendSwitch('enable-features', 'OverlayScrollbar')` called before `app.whenReady()` should enable overlay scrollbars for all windows, as it did in Electron 43.x\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nAfter upgrading to Electron 44.x, all windows still render classic scrollbars.\n\n`app.commandLine.getSwitchValue('enable-features')` returns `OverlayScrollbar`, so the switch itself is set correctly, but it has no effect.\n\n### Testcase Gist URL\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional Information\n\nYou can use an AI coding assistant and simply ask it to enable the overlay scrollbar in Electron.",
